---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';

const headings = [
  { id: 'requirements', text: 'Requirements', level: 2 },
  { id: 'releases', text: 'GitHub Releases', level: 2 },
  { id: 'homebrew', text: 'Homebrew', level: 2 },
  { id: 'development', text: 'Development builds', level: 2 },
];
---

<DocsLayout title="Installation" headings={headings}>
  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>macOS:</strong> Apple Silicon or Intel; native build jobs are prepared for both architectures.</li>
    <li><strong>Linux:</strong> experimental x86_64 builds for an X11/Wayland desktop with Vulkan graphics and the required system libraries.</li>
    <li><strong>Windows:</strong> experimental x86_64 build job; native editor, clipboard, IME, and recovery-directory privacy/locking acceptance remain pending.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="releases">GitHub Releases</h2>
  <p>Successful branch builds provide 14-day Actions artifacts; matching version tags publish checksum-backed GitHub Releases after all gates pass. The v0.8.1 release is the first macOS in-app update test target. Confirm available downloads on the releases page before installing.</p>
  <p>On macOS, the application menu checks for new stable releases automatically or on demand. Download and restart require your confirmation; unsaved drafts in every window must be checkpointed first. In-app replacement is not supported on Windows or Linux yet. macOS bundles are ad-hoc signed, not Developer-ID signed or notarized.</p>
  <p>Follow the <a href="https://github.com/alexey-a-abramov/markrust/releases">releases page</a> for public downloads. No current download link is implied by the prepared workflows.</p>
  <Callout type="note">
    <p>The prepared macOS bundles are ad-hoc signed, not Developer-ID signed or notarized. Windows archives are explicitly experimental and unsigned. Gatekeeper or SmartScreen may warn or block these development builds.</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="homebrew">Homebrew</h2>
  <p>The Homebrew tap is not published yet. It will be available after release archives and their checksums are published.</p>

  <h2 id="development">Development builds</h2>
  <p>Until binary downloads are published, developers can use the <a href="/docs/building">source-build instructions</a>, including platform toolchains and Cargo installation. These are development workflows, not a one-click end-user installer.</p>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <p><a href="/docs/building">Building from source</a> · <a href="/docs/roadmap">Release gates</a> · <a href="https://github.com/alexey-a-abramov/markrust/blob/main/docs/deployment.md">Distribution reference</a></p>
</DocsLayout>
